# Pure OO Philosophy Demo - Everything is a message!

Greeter:
    String name
    
    setName(String n):
        this.name = n
    
    greet():
        "Hello, ".print()
        this.name.print()
        "!".println()

Int main():
        "=== Atom: Pure Object-Oriented ===".println()
        "".println()
        
        "In Atom, everything is an object.".println()
        "Even strings respond to messages!".println()
        "".println()
        
        "Examples:".println()
        "  \"text\".println()   # String receives println message".println()
        "  \"text\".print()     # String receives print message".println()
        "".println()
        
        "This follows Smalltalk's philosophy:".println()
        "  - Pure message passing".println()
        "  - No global functions".println()
        "  - Objects respond to messages".println()
        "".println()
        
        "Just like 1 + 2 is really 1.add(2),".println()
        "printing is message.println()!".println()
        
        return 0
